# Adventure Works — Power BI Report

> **4 years of transactional data · Profit-first analytics · 2 interactive dashboards**

---

## Overview

This Power BI report (`Adventure_work.pbix`) analyzes Adventure Works transactional data spanning four years. The primary objective is to understand **profit performance** across three analytical dimensions: **time trends**, **products**, and **customer geography**.

The report is split into two dashboards, each answering a distinct set of business questions through interactive visuals and custom Power BI components.

---

## File Structure

```
Adventure_work.pbix
├── Dashboard 1 — Time Analysis Dashboard
├── Dashboard 2 — Detail Dashboard
```



## Dashboard 1 — Time Analysis Dashboard

Focuses on **how profit and revenue have changed over time** — by year, quarter, month, week type, and day.

### Visuals Included

| # | Visual | Description |
|---|--------|-------------|
| 1 | **KPI Cards vs. Previous Year** | Side-by-side comparison of COGS, Revenue, Quantity, Profit, Profit Margin, and Transaction count against prior year values |
| 2 | **Yearly Performance (Above Average)** | Column chart highlighting years where Revenue, Profit, and Transactions exceeded the overall average |
| 3 | **Monthly Profit Trend** | Line chart tracking monthly profit across all 4 years — reveals seasonality and growth patterns |
| 4 | **Profit by Week Type** | Donut chart splitting profit between weekday and weekend sales |
| 5 | **Quarterly Profit Analysis** |Advanced Cards comparing Q1–Q4 performance, with custom quarter icons |
| 6 | **Profit by Weekday** | Bar chart breaking profit down by day of the week (Mon–Sun) |

### Key Questions Answered
- Which years outperformed the average?
- Is profit growing month-over-month?
- Does the business perform better on weekdays or weekends?
- Which quarter and which day of the week drive the most profit?

---

## Dashboard 2 — Detail Dashboard

Focuses on **what drives profit** — products, customer demographics, geography, and pricing.

### Visuals Included

| # | Visual | Description |
|---|--------|-------------|
| 1 | **Top 5 Products by Profit** | Treemap + % breakdown of the five most profitable products vs. all others |
| 2 | **Top 5 Customers by Profit** | Top five high-value customers with % share of total profit |
| 3 | **Profit by Gender** | Pie chart comparing male vs. female customer profit contribution |
| 4 | **Profit by Product Color** | Bar chart highlighting best-selling product colors by profit |
| 5 | **Profit by Pricing Type** | Scatter Plot. |
| 6 | **Country-wise Profit (Map)** | Azure Map visual plotting profit distribution by country |
| 7 | **Profit by Age Group** | Table showing profit contribution by customer age demographic |

### Key Questions Answered
- Which products generate the most profit?
- Do male or female customers generate more profit?
- Which countries are most profitable?
- Which age group is the primary profit driver?

---

## Core Measures & KPIs

| Measure | Formula |
|---------|---------|
| **Profit** | Revenue − COGS |
| **Profit Margin** | Profit / Revenue × 100 |
| **Revenue** | SUM of transaction sale values |
| **COGS** | Cost of goods sold |
| **Quantity** | Total units sold |
| **Transactions** | Count of order rows |
| **PY Profit** | Profit for the previous year (time intelligence) |

---

## Analytical Dimensions

- **Time** — Year, Quarter, Month, Week Type (weekday/weekend), Day of Week
- **Product** — Product Name, Color, Pricing Type
- **Customer** — Gender, Age Group
- **Customer** — Country/Geography

---

## Interactive Filters

The report includes the following slicers for cross-dashboard filtering:

- Year selector
- Month range
- Country / Region

---

## How to Use

1. Open `Adventure_work.pbix` in **Power BI Desktop** (version with Azure Map support recommended).
2. Navigate between dashboards using the **Page Navigator** buttons at the Top of each page.
3. Use the **slicers** (filters) on  each dashboard to drill into specific time periods or regions.

---

## Requirements

- Power BI Desktop (latest version recommended)
- Internet connection required for the **Azure Map** visual on Dashboard 2
- Custom visuals are bundled inside the `.pbix` file — no separate installation needed

